{"title":"Career Roadmap: Process Control Engineer","role":"Process Control Engineer","summary":"A Process Control Engineer works on automated systems that control industrial processes in sectors such as:","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E. (Bachelor of Technology / Engineering)","Course":"Electronics & Instrumentation Engineering (EIE)"},"about":[{"label":"Primary Goal","text":"Design, configure, optimize and maintain automated control systems used to monitor and regulate industrial processes"}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Roadmap Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Process Control Engineer works on automated systems that control industrial processes in sectors such as:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Oil & gas"},{"text":"Petrochemicals"},{"text":"Chemicals"},{"text":"Pharmaceuticals"},{"text":"Power generation"},{"text":"Food processing"},{"text":"Manufacturing"},{"text":"Water treatment"},{"text":"Mining"},{"text":"Cement and metals"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The core progression is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Instrumentation","Sensors","Measurement","Control Theory","PLC/DCS","SCADA","Industrial Networks","Process Automation","Advanced Control","Industrial Optimization"]},{"type":"p","text":"For an EIE student, the strongest combination is instrumentation fundamentals + control theory + industrial automation + process knowledge."}]},{"heading":"What to Build During UG","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Year","Build This","Learn From","Proof of Progress","Gap It Moves"],"rows":[[{"text":"1st Year"},{"text":"Mathematics, programming, basic electrical/electronics"},{"text":"MIT OpenCourseWare","url":"https://ocw.mit.edu/"},{"text":"C/Python + circuit projects"},{"text":"Engineering foundation"}],[{"text":"2nd Year"},{"text":"Sensors, measurement systems, transducers"},{"text":"NPTEL","url":"https://nptel.ac.in/"},{"text":"Sensor calibration and measurement projec